5. The "jack in the box" metaphor — and where it lives

Your phrase is exactly right. A jack in the box is a surprising eruption — something pops out when you crank the handle.

The jack-in-the-box is the V8 Causal Engine. It's the thing that chains rules together and produces a conclusion that wasn't stored anywhere.

Example:

· You ask: "Why did the Roman Empire fall?"
· V7 (World Model): identifies Rome, identifies the year 476, identifies the region.
· V8 (Causal Engine): chains rules — "economic strain causes political instability, political instability causes military weakness, military weakness invites invasion."
· The council produces a causal chain.

That's not a fact. That's a narrative. The council constructs it from primitives.

