6. What I'd add to the roadmap

Three notes:

Design Note 7 — The Ten Primitives (V7)
Every fact in the World Model is an instance of one of ten relationship primitives: Identity, Category, Containment, Composition, Attribute, Time, Causation, Similarity, Association, Negation.

Design Note 8 — Small Tree, Big Network (V7)
The World Model holds the skeleton of knowledge, not the content. Content is fetched from Wikipedia/Wikidata on demand. Inference emerges from structure + fetch + compute.

Design Note 9 — The Safety Boundary on Inference (V7)
The council may only state causal inferences that are explicitly defined in the rules. It may not infer causation from correlation. It may not generalize about human populations. This is a constitutional boundary, not a technical limitation.

